{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Managing the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Keeping Everyone Happy"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "May (just) As Well/Might (just) As Well"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">may as well</span> and <span class=\"strong\">might as well</span> to make suggestions. You use these phrases to suggest what you think is the easiest or most logical choice in a situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">may as well</span> when the situation you are talking about is fairly certain.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I am off for the day. I may as well do all my Christmas shopping today</span>. = I am certain to be off today. I can do my Christmas shopping."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">might as well</span> to suggest a higher level of uncertainty. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: I<span class=\"italic\">'m not sure when I'll get another break, so I might as well do my Christmas shopping today</span>. = I'm not sure whether I'll have a break at another point in time, so I should do my Christmas shopping."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might as well harness the power of the bright minds you employ. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may as well sit down with your team on a regular basis and brainstorm ideas. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might as well share that with the team and give them a pat on the back to show the team the value of their efforts and your appreciation. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may just as well find that people want to be a part of that and will be motivated by it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note: The phrase <span class=\"italic\">just as well</span> means a good or fortunate thing."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Using Should, Ought to, and Had Better "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use modals like <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to </span> or <span class=\"strong\">had better</span> to give advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common modals for giving advice are: <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">had better<span class=\"italic\">."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice. You also use <span class=\"strong\">should</span> for questions.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span> is used for giving strong advice.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Had better</span> is much stronger than either <span class=\"strong\">should</span> or <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>. It is used to give an order or to suggest that something negative will happen if you refuse the advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following structures:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main Verb + Advice</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">should/shouldn't</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">talk</span> to the customers nicely.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ought to </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">focus</span> on the service.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">had better</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">keep</span> our customers happy.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You had better share your successes and celebrate your accomplishments by rewarding your hard-working staff on a job well done.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should ask your staff what they would like to see."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to envision the ideal workplace."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'd better increase employee motivation further by offering incentives."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "motivation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "eagerness and willingness to do something without needing to be told or forced to do it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many restaurateurs are going green, but employee motivation may not be the first thing that comes to mind."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when motivating your staff."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to harness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use the natural force or power of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You might as well harness the power of the bright minds you employ. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to arm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide all the information, skills, or equipment you need to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You ought to arm your employees with the power to use their skills and ideas to implement change."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to increase"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become bigger in amount, number, or degree "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'd better increase employee motivation further by offering incentives to the person that comes up with the most innovative idea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reward "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give something to someone because they have done something good or helpful or have worked for it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You had better share your successes and celebrate your accomplishments by rewarding your hard-working staff on a job well done."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to result"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something happen "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Creating a workplace that cares about the environment generates a feeling of pride among your employees which will result in a team that is excited about coming to work"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search online for the TED talk by Michael Norton \u201cHow to Buy Happiness\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Watch the video and take notes of the main ideas. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Watch the video a second time and you can use the transcript for extra help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short summary of what Michael Norton says in his talk. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include details about how money can make people and any new terms that he introduces."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share these ideas with your family and friends. What do they think? What did you think about the ideas presented in his talk? "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I watch a video about happiness."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes of the main ideas. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a summary of the ideas presented. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share these ideas with family and friends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I offer my own opinions about the talk."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you stay motivated at school or work? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are you usually motivated by?"}, {"type": "Le